From: steamlink-ps5
Subject: data channel: hold partial frames ~1s so retransmits can land

The window discarded any frame older than 200 ms and the video layer abandoned
a half-assembled frame after 150 ms. Both are shorter than a round trip on a
weak Wi-Fi link, so a packet asked for by the new retransmission request
(0010) arrived after its frame had already been thrown away, and the client
spent many seconds cycling keyframe requests before one happened to complete
intact. Raise both to ~1 s: a retransmitted fragment now lands in time and the
frame finishes. This trades a little latency for not freezing, which is the
right call on a link that drops packets.

diff -ru a/src/session/channels/ch_data.c b/src/session/channels/ch_data.c
--- a/src/session/channels/ch_data.c	2026-10-08 21:28:11.454204946 -0700
+++ b/src/session/channels/ch_data.c	2026-10-08 21:28:11.466548920 -0700
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
 
 #include "ihs_buffer_ext.h"
 
-#define DISCARD_DIFF IHS_SESSION_PACKET_TIMESTAMP_FROM_MILLIS(200)
+#define DISCARD_DIFF IHS_SESSION_PACKET_TIMESTAMP_FROM_MILLIS(1000)
 
 static void DataThreadWorker(IHS_SessionChannelData *channel);
 
diff -ru a/src/session/channels/video/ch_data_video.c b/src/session/channels/video/ch_data_video.c
--- a/src/session/channels/video/ch_data_video.c	2026-10-08 21:28:11.449064061 -0700
+++ b/src/session/channels/video/ch_data_video.c	2026-10-08 21:28:11.466697553 -0700
@@ -371,8 +371,10 @@
     if (head == NULL || head == tail) {
         return;
     }
-    // 150 ms in 1/65536-second units. Span between oldest and newest pending fragment.
-    const uint32_t overflowSpan = (uint32_t) (150 * 65536 / 1000);
+    // 1000 ms in 1/65536-second units. Span between oldest and newest pending
+    // fragment: long enough that a retransmitted fragment can still land on a
+    // slow Wi-Fi link before the half-assembled frame is abandoned.
+    const uint32_t overflowSpan = (uint32_t) (1000 * 65536 / 1000);
     uint32_t span = tail->timestamp - head->timestamp;
     if (span <= overflowSpan) {
         return;
